A mark made while a view is detached is still a mark.

-[NSView setNeedsDisplay:] records the flag on the view and then tells the window, by sending
setViewsNeedDisplay: to [self window]. For a view whose tree is still being assembled that window
is nil, the message goes nowhere, and the view is left dirty with nothing that will ever notice.
The next display pass walks from the window and finds a flag no window was told about.

It is not a rare corner. iTerm2 3.5 marks its terminal view 482 times in one run and 313 of those
arrive before the view has a window, measured with the CIDER_NEEDSDISPLAY trace, which prints the
window number or -1.

Joining a window is the moment to deliver them, so _setWindow: now tells the new window when the
view it is adopting is already dirty. It recurses into subviews, so a whole subtree assembled
offscreen and then installed delivers every mark it accumulated.

WHAT IT DOES NOT FIX: iTerm2 3.5, measured before and after at 482 marks and 1 traversal redraw.
Its windowless marks all arrive before the first attach, and that attach already redraws the view
once, so there is nothing left for this to deliver. Task #239 has the evidence that the remaining
fault there is inside the application.

Gates: run-dts-batch, buck-bundled-patch-record-check, roster-sweep and roster-input.

--- a/AppKit/NSView.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSView.m
@@ -1816,6 +1816,16 @@
             [_layerContext setSubwindow: [_window _createSubWindowWithFrame: [self frame]]];
         }
 
+        /* A MARK MADE WHILE DETACHED IS STILL A MARK. setNeedsDisplay: records it on the view and
+         * then sends setViewsNeedDisplay: to [self window], which is nil for a view whose tree is
+         * still being assembled: the view stays dirty and no window ever hears about it, so it is
+         * never redrawn. iTerm2 3.5 marks its terminal view 482 times in a run and 313 of those
+         * arrive before the view has a window. Joining a window is the moment to deliver them.
+         * Task #239. */
+        if (_window != nil && _needsDisplay) {
+            [_window setViewsNeedDisplay: YES];
+        }
+
